# Go
/bin/
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Wails
/build/bin/
/build/windows/*.syso
# wails3 generate icons always emits a mac .icns even for this Windows-only
# project; the task diverts it into build/windows purely as a scratch output
/build/windows/icons.icns
/wails_windows_amd64.syso
# NOTE: build/windows/nsis/ is *source* (hand-maintained installer scripts),
# not build output — it must stay tracked, otherwise a fresh clone cannot
# build the installer. Wails' own generated template lives nowhere: the
# pipeline runs `makensis build/windows/nsis/installer.nsi` directly.

# Installer / packaged output
/dist/

# Frontend
frontend/node_modules/
# Keep the directory itself tracked (with .gitkeep) so `//go:embed all:frontend/dist`
# in main.go resolves on a fresh clone / CI checkout before the frontend is built.
frontend/dist/*
!frontend/dist/.gitkeep
frontend/**/node_modules/
node_modules/

# E2E
e2e/test-results/
e2e/artifacts/
e2e/playwright-report/

# Test coverage output (`npm run test:coverage` writes one report per workspace)
frontend/**/coverage/

# Headless export verification output (`--headless-export` smoke runs)
/build/verification/

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log

# Worktrees
.worktrees/

# Tool caches / temp
.task/
.trae-html-share-packages/
.screenshots/
.workbuddy/
# Icon source backups (regenerate with `task generate:icons`)
.icon-backup/
# Playwright run output from a test invocation that did not run inside e2e/
/test-results/
# genoffice site-asset tool state (regenerated on next tool run)
site/assets/.genoffice-assets.json

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
